sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch03-26> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "In brine-shrimps (Artemia), increasing salinity changes the relative rates of growth of body parts, the abdomen growing relatively longer compared with the cephalothorax the salter the water, so that forms described as distinct species correspond to ranges of water density.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Brine-shrimp abdomen grows relatively longer the saltier the water";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter III, “The Rate of Growth”; topic “Osmotic factors in growth”. Scope: brine-shrimps (Artemia) in waters of varying salinity"
}
